  "schema_version": 1,
  "note": "Fixed-literal language markers, matched as bytes, never decoded. A hit is one mechanism and is not a language claim: settleLanguage pairs it with a symbol mangling family on disjoint ranges and emit decides. corpus names the artifact the literal was read from; buildSigpack refuses a missing or weak atom, and 26 of 35 rules carry no corpus yet, so their literals are previewed but unverified - treat those as leads, not evidence. DIE db markers (db/*/_*.sg, MIT) informed the C++/Delphi families; no ClamAV GPL data is embedded.",
